# Node-only tooling. Pushing these breaks the GAS project at parse time:
# 'require is not defined' fires before ANY function runs, so every diag and
# every form dies. tools-deadscan.js did exactly that on 2026-08-13.
tools-*.node
# .node is Node's NATIVE-BINARY extension and cannot be require()d as JS.
# Node-only tooling uses .cjs instead, still excluded from the GAS push.
tools-*.cjs

# Shadow duplicates: Drive sync creates "Foo (1).js" beside "Foo.js". Every .js
# in a GAS project shares ONE global scope and the last file parsed wins, so a
# stale copy can silently REPLACE production code. Measured on 2026-08-14: the
# shadows were divergent OLDER versions — "OQC (1).js" defaulted AQL to level II
# where OQC.js uses I (a different number of units inspected on a release), had
# no idempotency guard, and "ProductionReadCache (1).js" was MISSING six
# functions the real one defines, which would be a ReferenceError if it won.
# Ignored here as well as deleted, so a future Drive sync cannot re-ship them.
**/*(1).js
**/*(2).js
**/*(1).html
**/*(2).html
**/* (1).js
**/* (2).js
**/* (1).html
**/* (2).html
